<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alonso de Ojeda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1466–1515</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Alonso de Hojeda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alonso de Ojeda was a Spanish explorer who sailed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>'s second voyage in 1493. On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> he captured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> cacique <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caonabo">Caonabo</a> by a ruse in 1495. He later led voyages along the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, naming Venezuela in 1499, and tried to found a colony at San Sebastián de Urabá in 1510, before dying poor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alonso-de-ojeda.jpg" alt="Alonso de Ojeda" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ignacio Castillo Cervantes · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conquistador_Alonso_de_Ojeda.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
